menu "OpenHaunt audio"
    config OH_AUDIO
        bool "Audio output: stored clips and an RTP stream (OpenHaunt/node doc 13)"
        default y if OH_BOARD_OH_NODE_V0
        default n
        depends on SPIRAM
        help
            Needs the board's I2S pins (OpenHaunt board menu), PSRAM for the
            stream's buffer and the clip readers, and a FAT partition named
            "clips" in the partition table.

    config OH_AUDIO_AMP_ALWAYS_ON
        bool "Keep the speaker amplifier on while nothing plays"
        depends on OH_AUDIO
        default y if OH_BOARD_OH_NODE_V0_1
        default n
        help
            A MAX98357A in shutdown leaves its outputs high-impedance. V0.1 wires
            them to a 3.5 mm jack that usually feeds another amplifier, whose input
            then floats and hums. On, the amplifier stays powered and is fed
            silence, which holds the line at zero. Off, it is powered just ahead
            of a sound and dropped two seconds after, which V0.2's power-bank
            budget wants.

    config OH_AUDIO_SWAP_LR
        bool "Swap left and right on the way out"
        depends on OH_AUDIO
        default y if OH_BOARD_OH_NODE_V0_2
        default n
        help
            V0.2's STX-3000 footprint has its T and R pads named the wrong way
            round, so the left channel comes out of the ring. Found on the first
            board on 2026-10-26; the footprint is fixed for the next revision,
            and this puts the boards already built right in the meantime.

    config OH_AUDIO_CLIPS_PARTITION
        string "Partition label of the clip store"
        depends on OH_AUDIO
        default "clips"
endmenu
